<title>USA: CORESTAFF Inc Q1 net income rises.</title>
<headline>CORESTAFF Inc Q1 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>					   Historical  Pro Forma</p>
<p>				     1997	1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		     $216,948 $103,386 $223,264 $171,357</p>
<p> Gross profit		   49,855   25,702   52,311   41,039</p>
<p> Operating  income	    12,221    5,826   12,965   10,204</p>
<p> Net  income		     5,755    2,669    6,035    3,355</p>
<p> Earnings per common share    0.18     0.10     0.19     0.12</p>
<p> Avg shrs outstanding	 32,429   27,339   32,429   27,339</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: The average number of shares outstanding during the current quarter was 19 percent higher than a year ago, as a result of a follow-on public offering in May 1996.</p>
<p>Pro forma operating results assume all acquisitions consummated through March 31, 1997, and the sale of the physical therapy staffing business in January 1997 occurred as of the beginning of the periods presented.</p>
</text>
